4.1 Hypertension in disaster, humanitarian and emergency settings
Hypertension (HTN) is seen in a range of humanitarian crises and disaster settings (natural or 
humanmade). This includes, but is not limited to, the wars in Syria and Iraq, the impact of the Great 
East Japan Earthquake and Hurricane Katrina, and the living conditions of Palestinian refugees. The 
burden of HTN on those populations can be considerable (82). There are very little data on HTN control, 
